# Concord code owners.
#
# GitHub requests a review from everyone matched here when a pull request
# touches a matching path. Two maintainers read the whole tree, so one catch-all
# rule is the whole file: per-directory rules would name the same two people and
# only add places to forget when one of them changes.
#
# MAINTAINERS.md says which changes need BOTH approvals rather than one. GitHub
# cannot express that, so it stays a rule we keep, not one that is enforced.
#
# Both maintainers are requested on every pull request. A CODEOWNERS rule that
# names an account GitHub cannot resolve is treated as an error and applies
# nothing, so keep these handles correct.

